Requirements: 33   with obligations: 32   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Obligation pairs too dissimilar to state one requirement are not asked about.
    -> obligation-distance-threshold-exclusion  [functional/explicit]   (also serves constraint-03)
       Pairs whose distance exceeds the threshold are not sent to the model.
    -> task-01-obligation-2  [functional/inferred]
       Pairs are filtered for asking based on cosine distance between their embeddings.
    -> task-01-obligation-4  [functional/inferred]
       The threshold used for filtering is configurable and defaults to 0.10.

[constraint-01] Each obligation is embedded as a vector.
    -> obligation-embeddings-per-obligation  [functional/explicit]
       Each obligation is represented as a vector embedding.

[constraint-02] The distance between two obligations is the cosine distance between
    their embeddings.
    -> obligation-cosine-distance  [functional/explicit]
       The distance between two obligations is computed as cosine distance between their
       embeddings.

[constraint-03] A pair whose distance exceeds a threshold is never sent to the model.
    -> obligation-distance-threshold-exclusion  [functional/explicit]   (also serves task-01)
       Pairs whose distance exceeds the threshold are not sent to the model.

[constraint-04] A pair whose distance is within the threshold is sent to the model.
    -> obligation-distance-threshold-inclusion  [functional/explicit]
       Pairs whose distance is within the threshold are sent to the model.

[constraint-05] The threshold is configurable.
    -> obligation-threshold-configurable  [docs_config/explicit]
       The threshold is configurable.

[constraint-06] The threshold defaults to 0.10.
    -> obligation-threshold-default-010  [functional/explicit]
       The threshold defaults to 0.10.

[constraint-07] A pair excluded for stating a different kind of demand stays excluded
    whatever its distance.
    -> pair-excluded-for-demand-stays-excluded  [invariant/explicit]
       A pair excluded for stating a different kind of demand remains excluded
       regardless of its distance.

[constraint-08] The number of pairs excluded by distance is recorded.
    -> distance-exclusion-count-recorded  [functional/explicit]
       The number of pairs excluded by distance is recorded.

[constraint-09] The threshold in force is recorded.
    -> threshold-in-force-recorded  [functional/explicit]
       The threshold in force is recorded.

[constraint-10] Both records are part of the persisted review state.
    -> records-persisted-review-state  [invariant/explicit]
       Both the distance-exclusion count record and the threshold-in-force record are
       part of the persisted review state.

[constraint-11] An embedding request is recorded for replay.
    -> embedding-request-recorded-for-replay  [functional/explicit]
       An embedding request is recorded for replay.

[constraint-12] An embedding request is replayed rather than issued again once it has a
    recording.
    -> embedding-request-replayed-from-recording  [regression/explicit]
       An embedding request is replayed rather than issued again once it has a
       recording.

[constraint-13] Changing the threshold invalidates the recorded linking requests.
    -> threshold-change-invalidates-recorded-linking-requests  [invariant/explicit]
       Changing the threshold invalidates the recorded linking requests.

[constraint-14] Changing the embedding model invalidates the recorded linking requests.
    -> embedding-model-change-invalidates-recorded-linking-requests  [invariant/explicit]
       Changing the embedding model invalidates the recorded linking requests.

[constraint-15] Two runs over the same obligation set choose the same pairs.
    -> same-pairs-same-obligation-set  [invariant/explicit]
       Two runs over the same obligation set choose the same pairs.

[constraint-16] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
